  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": ".NET 8 through .NET 11 selected collection additions",
      "items": [
        ".NET 8 added FrozenDictionary<TKey,TValue> and FrozenSet<T> for collections created infrequently and read frequently. .NET 9 added alternate-key lookup support to Dictionary<TKey,TValue> and HashSet<T> for compatible alternate key types. Confirm the target framework before using these APIs.",
        "ConcurrentDictionary alternate-key lookup APIs are available starting in .NET 9 when its comparer supports IAlternateEqualityComparer<TAlternateKey,TKey>."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.frozen",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.generic.dictionary-2",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/whats-new/dotnet-8/overview",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/whats-new/dotnet-9/overview",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.concurrent.concurrentdictionary-2.getalternatelookup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "C# 12 and C# 15",
      "items": [
        "C# 12 introduced target-typed collection expressions, spread elements, and collection-builder support. C# 15 added the leading with(...) element to pass arguments to a collection constructor or builder. The with(...) arguments do not select the target type during overload resolution; verify compiler language version separately from target framework."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-reference/operators/collection-expressions",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/csharp-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": ".NET 9 through .NET 11",
      "items": [
        "The generic OrderedDictionary<TKey,TValue> provides key lookup plus explicit insertion-order/index operations; it is available from .NET 9. Use it when insertion order and key lookup are both required, not when keys must be sorted."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.collections.generic.ordereddictionary-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": ".NET 11",
